      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَاشِكٌ</span></b>  [act. part. n. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَشَكَ</span>]. You say <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَاةٌ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَاشِكَةٌ</span> <i>A sheep,</i> or <i>goat, abounding with milk.</i>
(TA in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لجب</span>.) [And hence,] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَخْلَةٌ حَاشِكٌ</span>
(tropical:)  <i>A palm-tree bearing much fruit.</i> (Yaakoob, S,
K.) ― 
